  <cac:TenderingProcess>
    
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">The procurement is for contracts. 6, ventilation. The works concern ventilation works in connection with the construction of a new extension. This also includes alterations to the air intake in the existing building, as well as some channel work in the heating plant. Three balanced ventilation systems shall be delivered in the extension. Two systems primarily cover resident rooms and one system cover common areas and personnel rooms etc. This system has full needs management, whilst the systems for the resident rooms have zone control. There is also an exhaust system for lift machine rooms and a exhaust system from a heat pump (the fan is delivered with the heat pump) where the assembly is included in this delivery.  A fire philosophy will be set up in the building with a bypass outside of the filter and rotor, but there is still a lot of fire damper due to a sectioning wall in two places in the extension, where all fire sellers south of the sectioning wall must be equipped with a fire damper. The ventilation aggregates are to be delivered without automation. Automation is included in the electro contract.</cbc:Description>
    <cbc:ProcedureCode listName="procurement-procedure-type">neg-w-call</cbc:ProcedureCode>
    <cac:ProcessJustification>
      <cbc:ProcessReasonCode listName="accelerated-procedure">false</cbc:ProcessReasonCode>
    </cac:ProcessJustification>
  </cac:TenderingProcess>
  <cac:ProcurementProject>
    <cbc:ID>2025/4151</cbc:ID>
    
    <cbc:Name languageID="ENG">Expansion of Kvernaland welfare centre - ventilation - EP06</cbc:Name>
    
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">Time municipality shall expand Kvernaland welfare centre with 27 new places. The places shall be organised as book collectives, divided in three departments. Each department consists of nine bed rooms connected to a common living room. The extension shall be adapted to the user group, which primarily consists of elderly persons with dementia, and emphasis will be put on a homely design, good accessibility and robust solutions. The tenders will be published as joint contracts, this tender documentation is for timber. Address: Gamle Åslandsvegen 27, 4355 KvernalandOn the property Gamle Åslandsvegen 25-27, there are the following existing buildings: Children and respite care home with seven places, moved in March 2015Care centre with 24 places, moved in September 2015, Parent initiative with 7 places, moved in January 2017 The expansion is formed as a horse shoe, partly on one floor and partly over two floors. The total area of use (BRA) for the expansion is 2,156 m². A closed sensory garden will form a closed sensory garden with an outer wall in the existing sheltered care centre. In addition: A joint shed with superstructure bicycle parking (BRA: 129 m²) Expansion of the technical building (approx. 15 m²) HVAC installations, An outdoor facility with expanded parking for both bicycles and car Development of a sensory garden and other outside areas shall be constructed.</cbc:Description>
